#!args scenario=Scenario_OneRound seed=42
#
# Regression: RecycleDestination.ShuffleIntoDeck must actually shuffle the draw deck.
#
# DeckState.ShuffleDeck() used to be `DeckCardIds.Shuffle();`. The Shuffle extension returns a NEW
# list and does not mutate, so the result was discarded and the deck was left in its original order:
# the recycled card was appended to the bottom and the deck was called shuffled.
#
# `decktop` is what catches it. With the bug the top card cannot move, because appending to the
# bottom never touches it. The replicated state hash cannot catch this at all — it covers the deck
# COUNT, not the order (see MultiplayerGameState.ComputeHash, `d{deck.DeckCardIds.Count}`), which is
# also why the fix has to put the host's shuffled order on the wire instead of letting each peer
# shuffle for itself.
#
# Values below are pinned to the seed in the #!args line above; they are deterministic given it.
# Run:  tests/run-cli.sh tests/qgc/shuffle_into_deck.qgc

prompt                                  # turn 1, Germany, PLAY_CARD
pass
prompt                                  # DISCARD step
discard 1                               # discard Guns and Butter (card 0)

# Recycling out of the discard pile is what every in-game caller does, so that is the path pinned
# here. Recycling from elsewhere is covered by recycle_moves_card.qgc.
assert card 0 in discard
assert decksize GERMANY == 25
assert decktop GERMANY == 8

api recycleCard --faction GERMANY --card 0 --destination ShuffleIntoDeck

assert card 0 in deck
assert decksize GERMANY == 26
assert decktop GERMANY != 8             # FAILS if the shuffle is a no-op

quit
